WEBVTT

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.660
What do you want?

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.880
I was in the area, so I thought 
I should say hello.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.170
Of course, I don't expect you to believe it.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.380
What is that?

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.420
Info on the Dreams of Alice.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.280
Fine, I'll take it. But it's too soon.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.890
We can't cover it up any longer.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.910
You came up with this yourself?

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.950
Let's just say I acted on my own authority.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.900
How very valiant, for a lizard's tail.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.830
If it becomes necessary, you'll be cut off.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.780
Well, even tails have their 
own sense of pride.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.010
<b>I'm Home</b>

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.340
<b>Searching for This Girl! 

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:43.050
<i>It's been ten days since Ha-chan disappeared.</i>

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.120
<i>It'll be April soon.</i>

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:45.870
Shoot!

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:46.470
Get back!

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.430
Nice, Ayumu.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.600
Nice, Ayumu!

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.690
<b>Searching for Shikishima Hatori-chan</b>

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.690
<b>

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.690
<b>
Please Contact Us If You See Her</b>

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:57.400
<i>The police and all the adults 
have been looking for her.</i>

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.860
<i>But...</i>

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.450
<i>I don't think she's coming back.</i>

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.660
Hey, if you took a trip, where would you go?

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.920
I'm not sure. Where would you go?

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.840
Off the top of my head, I don't know.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.380
You can pick anywhere.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:18.840
Oh.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.460
Wait, I know.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.710
I'll try to guess.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.830
Liverpool, right?

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.240
I knew it.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.680
How did you know?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.620
You told me before, remember?

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.260
Because you like soccer.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.000
Did I say that?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.040
You did.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:38.160
There isn't anywhere you'd want to go?

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.720
Er, what?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:42.820
It's embarrassing...

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.090
Come on, no fair!

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:49.240
Well, um... When spring comes,

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.900
I want to follow the blooming flowers,

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.140
from south to all the way up north.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:03:59.650
Yeah.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.780
That sounds really cool!

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:03.590
Really co—

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:04.500
Jeez!

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.920
Ow, what's the worry? Let's go!

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:09.340
Let's go and do it together!

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.280
Yeah.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.930
We'll go together.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.240
<b>No Answer</b>

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:25.240
Ha-chan!

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:32.200
Answer!

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:33.900
Please!

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:38.870
Ha-chan...

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.960
You went by yourself?

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.650
<b>Missed Call</b>

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.040
If we ever get out of here,

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.600
will you forgive me?

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.620
Forgive you? For what?

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.950
I'm not mad about anything anymore.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.140
Then, will you be my friend?

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.180
I'll introduce you to my best friend, too.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.280
Your best friend?

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.170
You mean Ayumu? I already know her.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.180
She said you're her most 
precious friend, too.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:30.680
That's right... She's my very best friend.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.480
So, how do we look for the exit?

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.610
Well,

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.110
if we can find some clue to start...

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:42.990
Huh?

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.140
What's wrong?

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.530
I think I dropped my phone!

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:47.840
Huh?

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:48.990
I'll go back and...

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.490
My phone!

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.590
When did he—

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:53.530
Give that back!

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.330
You can't get away now!

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.670
<b>Ayu-chan</b>

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:05.670
Ayu-chan?

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.310
A minute ago, it was out of range!

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.090
Is it broken?

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:11.430
A call.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.460
I got a call from Ayu-chan.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.770
It should connect...

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.350
The rabbit is connected to the outside.

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.280
What? This thing?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.530
Hey, you!

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.400
Wait!

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.990
<b>Kashimura      Zoroku 
Sanae  
Sana</b>

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.700
Please come out.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:40.710
It's okay...

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.480
This is a mailbox.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:45.450
They open from the ba—

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:01.950
Hatori, wait.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:03.180
What?

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.310
Don't your feet hurt?

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.070
You should... put shoes on.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.280
Lots of them... are growing right there...

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.030
Oh...

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:16.420
I wonder where the rabbit went.

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:18.980
It's probably close.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.850
How do you know?

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.330
He's just... like me.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.390
He was made in Wonderland.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:28.440
He likes fun and weird things.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.890
So I'm sure he's teasing us, just having fun.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.700
There he is!

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:36.890
You little...

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:53.800
Why are there so many pancakes?

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.640
Well, Sana-chan loves pancakes.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.040
I hope Sana-chan's okay.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.120
I'll bet she's getting hungry...

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.930
H-Hatori, wait...

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.040
Are you all right?

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.080
I can't go any farther!

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.880
Me, neither!

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.210
You fell for it!

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:03.680
<b>Ha-chan 

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.640
Ha... Ha-chan!

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:08.480
Well? Did it send?

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.800
Hang on. I'm not sure yet.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.050
Give it here! I'll send a bunch of them!

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:16.750
You can't... The battery 
won't last that long.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:19.910
<b>Ayu-chan</b>

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.890
Hello, Ayu-chan? Can you hear me?

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:28.150
<i>Listen, I'm sorry, but I need your help.</i>

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.840
<i>Give me that! I wanna talk to her!</i>

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.140
Just wait...

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.080
<i>Ha-chan?</i>

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.670
<i>Is it really you, Ha-chan?</i>

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.300
Yeah, it's me.

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.320
Thank goodness...

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:40.300
I thought I'd never see you again.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.500
Huh?

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:45.520
<i>I mean, everyone's been 
looking, for over ten days!</i>

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.590
Over ten days? What does she mean?

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:50.900
What do you mean? What day is it?

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:52.780
<i>What day?</i>

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:56.740
<i>It's already March 29, Ha-chan!</i>

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:00.200
<i>Don't cry... I'm sorry.</i>

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.070
<i>I didn't know.</i>

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:07.250
I thought I'd made you angry...

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.840
<i>I thought you didn't like me anymore.</i>

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:16.610
So I'm sorry, but please 
don't come again.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.990
No, not at all... It's me.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:28.770
As your friend, I failed you.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.480
You've...

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.850
<i>always been my best, most precious friend,</i>

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:36.240
<i>who I love most of all.</i>

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.360
Yeah... Same here, Ha-chan.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:43.030
Wh-What's that?!

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.530
<b>Your battery power is low. 
10% remaining.</b>

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.530
<b>

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:44.260
The battery...

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.300
Hey, Ayu-chan, I have to be fast.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:48.980
I need you to look for a rabbit hole.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:49.540
Let me!

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.130
A rabbit hole?

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:52.310
<i>Hey, Ayumu!</i>

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.170
Kashimura-san?

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:58.480
<i>Listen, do you remember the rabbit 
you saw when we talked before?</i>

00:10:58.480 --> 00:10:59.500
Rabbit?

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:03.860
<i>Right now, Hatori and I can't use our powers.</i>

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:06.600
<i>And we can't get out of here.</i>

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:10.850
But that exit might still 
connect to the outside.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.490
<i>Wonderland is too big.</i>

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:14.920
<i>We can't find the exit from the inside.</i>

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:19.100
<i>But the outside world is smaller, 
and there are lots of signs.</i>

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.490
<i>We want to get home, fast!</i>

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.490
<b>Pedestrians and Bicycles Only</b>

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:23.250
<i>Please, Ayu-chan.</i>

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:25.750
Okay, I think I know where it is.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:29.000
And if I have any confidence, 
it's in my speed!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.140
<i>Wait for me!</i>

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.210
Think she'll be okay?

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.090
Yeah.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.100
Ayu-chan can handle it.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:41.640
I know that she'll save us.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:51.250
Grandpa, what is this?

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:54.100
A lunch box, I guess?

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.020
I can see that, but...

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.380
The day I first met her,

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.140
she was in the convenience 
store, staring at them.

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:08.620
This "Wonderland" sure is a weird place.

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:14.040
So this is where Sana-chan was born...

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:17.800
I suppose this is normal for her,

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.540
and the outside world seems strange.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.140
Since she left here,

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.970
she's been surrounded by unfamiliar things.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.610
For her, everything is a first.

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:34.350
And as she confronts each of those things,

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.480
she's learning how to associate with people.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.720
Come to think of it,

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.110
that's how I've always lived, too.

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:48.770
I've made it this far because of the 
help I received from others.

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:50.960
I guess that's true of me, too.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:54.700
When you receive something, 
you need to give back in kind.

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:55.520
Yeah.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:12:59.920
The pig!

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:06.600
It should be around here.

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:14.380
Come on, please.

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:16.190
My friend's waiting for me!

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.010
Come out.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.980
<b>Stop</b>

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:25.850
Please... Take me there!

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:29.030
What is this?

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.740
Why is there a door?

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:46.840
What... It disappeared?

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:49.580
What's going on?

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.380
It's expanding even faster!

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:54.430
I fear it will affect the surface 
sooner than we expected!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.050
Is there no way to stop it?

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:57.690
Senpai...

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:00.970
Hey, hasn't it been a while?

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.530
Does she really know where it is?

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:05.740
She does.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:08.110
Ayu-chan definitely knows.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.580
What makes you think that?

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:12.900
Huh? Well, I don't know the reason.

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:15.450
Because she's my friend, I guess?

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:19.840
Y-You guys say some similar things.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.580
Listen...

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:22.760
What?

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:25.610
Ayumu is your best friend,

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:28.870
and you're Ayumu's best friend, right?

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:29.710
Yeah.

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:31.390
Th-Then am I...

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:41.140
A-Ayu-chan!

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.270
Ha-chan!

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:45.770
Thank goodness!

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:50.850
Wait!

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:53.160
Huh?

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:56.410
I thought it was two, but I see three.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:59.920
Sana-chan... and a friend?

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:02.690
Sana-chan!

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:17.000
You think we can cross on this?

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:18.940
Whoa! What now?

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:20.810
Can we ride these?

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.480
How convenient!

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:24.230
H-Hey!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.200
What's that?

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:33.480
Zoroku, hurry!

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:36.270
<i>All staff, please begin evacuation.</i>

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.080
<i>Please begin evacuation.</i>

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.820
Wonderland is coming to the surface!

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:41.670
Research Building 3 is going to collapse!

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:43.920
Senpai! Senpai!

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.990
Yamada-san, what are you doing?

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.630
Didn't you hear the evacuation order?

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.270
But Senpai is still in Wonderland—

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:52.240
You can't! We don't know 
what's going on inside!

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:54.430
Senpai! Ichijo-senpai!

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.640
Zoroku!

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:57.970
What's happening?

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.710
I... I don't know, either.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:03.730
Looks like something big is about to happen.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.390
Zoroku!

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:10.900
You okay?

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:12.360
Yeah.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:14.390
Good.

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:27.280
Cut it out already!

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:30.070
<i>He really did give Wonderland a talking to.</i>

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:39.320
It's getting away.

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:43.940
Don't you still have something to do?

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.380
You want us to push that?

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:52.890
Grandpa, maybe he's just teasing us again.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:55.860
If so, he'll get another talking to.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.710
I thought so...

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:24.130
Ichijo-san!

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.600
What in the world is going on?

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:32.870
Wonderland's expansion has stopped!

00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:33.820
Yes...

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.250
We're saved!

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:39.710
Why did it stop?

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:46.220
Huh? Where is this?

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.790
It's my house! Yay!

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:51.260
It's my house!

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.710
Hey, Kashimura-san, your shoes...

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:54.170
Sana!

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:58.040
Start by taking off your shoes.

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:16.360
Senpai!

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:23.660
Is Wonderland still expanding?

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:24.700
It's stopped.

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:27.740
I see... That's good.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:29.860
Where are Kashimura-san and the rest?

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:32.890
They all made it back home safely.

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:33.820
Now...

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:37.630
I'm going to sleep for a bit...

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:49.690
Huh? It really has been ten days!

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:51.200
What's going on?

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.730
This is pretty screwed-up.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:56.750
But I found the door about 
thirty minutes ago.

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:58.000
I'm so glad.

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:01.110
Now your parents won't have to worry.

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:07.120
Um, I'll... go home with Ha-chan.

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:10.960
I'll walk you there, then.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:14.420
Is this your house?

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:15.740
Yes.

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:18.620
Thank you for walking us here.

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:21.520
Hey, it was close. Think nothing of it.

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.760
Um, I'm really sorry for all the trouble.

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:29.970
After I talk to my parents, 
I'll go to the police.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.100
I-I'll go, too!

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:36.460
You two do have a lot to atone for.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.300
That's still true,

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.390
but you have people on your side.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:44.120
If you get into any trouble, call us.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.790
Yeah! With Zoroku around, you'll be fine!

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.450
Be quiet for a minute.

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:49.960
Also,

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:54.420
I know someone who makes his living 
by helping troubled kids like you.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:55.940
Thanks.

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.340
Ha-chan, listen...

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.210
After you disappeared,

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:07.730
your parents searched for you, every day.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:13.340
Sana-chan...

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:14.740
I'd like to ask a favor.

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:15.770
What is it?

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:19.730
Could you stay here, just for a little while?

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:23.280
When you're with me, I can't lie.

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:26.580
I know! I promised, after all.

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.210
I'm your friend, too! Okay?

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:36.170
I'm home.

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:38.630
Hatori!

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:50.480
I'm sorry.

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:59.220
<i>So, I'll say it again, once more.</i>

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:01.770
<i>The Dreams of Alice Response Office</i>

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:04.360
<i>is in the preparation stage.</i>

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:08.920
<i>In so many words, the Kyoto Ferris 
wheels are a Dream of Alice, also.</i>

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:11.430
<i>The important thing to remember</i>

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:14.760
<i>is that the phenomenon 
called a "Dream of Alice"</i>

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:17.900
<i>can happen to anyone.</i>

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:23.210
<i>No one is special or more likely to 
experience it than anyone else.</i>

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:23.210
We're off!

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:25.740
<i>So, to protect these people's rights,</i>

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:30.680
<i>the government will open a 
special response office—</i>

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:32.450
Hey...

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:36.440
Hatori-chan ended up with the "Dream 
of Alice" they discussed on TV, right?

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.330
Will she be okay?

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:40.820
Oh, Hatori-chan is a good girl.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:45.320
The government finally made 
an official announcement

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:47.820
about the existence of the Dreams of Alice.

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:51.420
The world is about to change, isn't it?

00:21:54.430 --> 00:21:57.180
I do hope it's a positive change.

00:21:57.630 --> 00:22:00.080
Well, I'm sure things will work out.

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:07.990
If the kids are happy and healthy, 
that makes it a good world.

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:21.520
<i>In the future, what sort of adult 
will this girl become?</i>

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:28.820
<i>How will she retain the cuteness 
and innocence of childhood?</i>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:33.160
<b>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:33.160
<b>Kashimura Sana</b>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:33.160
<b>Kashimura Sana</b>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:33.160
<b>Sana</b>

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:33.650
<i>These are the things that Alice's 
older sister thought about.</i>

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:34.620
<b>Kashimura Sana</b>

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:34.620
<b>

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:34.620
<b>

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:36.890
<i>When Alice becomes an adult,</i>

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:42.000
<i>she will surely tell many 
strange, fanciful stories</i>

00:22:42.530 --> 00:22:46.260
<i>to small children, who look just like her.</i>

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:50.550
<b>Kashimura      Zoroku 
Sanae  
Sana</b>

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:50.550
<i>Among those tales, perhaps,</i>

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:53.760
<i>she might tell that story...</i>

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:56.220
<b>

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:56.220
<b>

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:56.220
<b>Shikishima Hatori, Miho Ayumu (3)</b>

00:22:55.530 --> 00:22:57.780
<i>The story of a wondrous land,</i>

00:22:57.780 --> 00:22:59.980
<i>which she dreamed of, long ago.</i>

00:23:00.630 --> 00:23:02.310
Sana-chan!

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:04.550
Morning!

00:23:04.550 --> 00:23:05.570
Okay, I'm off!

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:08.280
Watch for cars, you three.

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:09.850
Okay!

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:18.460
<b>This is ——</b>

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:22.920
<b>the story of a girl . . .</b>

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:28.590
<b>who continues to search for "herself," 
so that she can become a "me" ——</b>

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:32.220
<i>I'm all right, now.</i>

00:23:33.420 --> 00:23:35.040
<i>Thanks to you...</i>

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:37.340
<i>Zoroku.</i>
